/-!
# The Marcinkiewicz interpolation theorem

This file was automatically generated by Claude.

This file proves the **Marcinkiewicz (real) interpolation theorem** for subadditive operators,
Blueprint Lemma 2.3 (`lem:interpolation`) of `blueprints/discrete-sw.tex`, in textbook
generality and with explicit constants. It depends on Mathlib only.

## Setting

* Inputs are functions `f : α → E` on a measure space `(α, μ)` (`μ` s-finite), outputs are
  functions `T f : β → F` on a possibly different measure space `(β, ν)`; `E` and `F` are
  arbitrary normed additive groups (so vector-valued inputs and outputs, e.g.
  `EuclideanSpace ℂ (Fin k)`, are covered).
* `T : (α → E) → β → F` is only required to behave well on a class `D` of inputs:
  * `IsSublinearOn T D ν`: `‖T (f + g)‖ ≤ ‖T f‖ + ‖T g‖` `ν`-a.e. for `f, g ∈ D`;
  * `IsTruncationClosed D`: `f 𝟙_{‖f‖ > s}` and `f 𝟙_{‖f‖ ≤ s}` lie in `D` for `f ∈ D`, `s > 0`
    (e.g. `D = univ`, `isTruncationClosed_univ`, or `D = L^q`, `isTruncationClosed_memLp`).
  Homogeneity is not needed.
* `distributionFunction g t ν = ν {x | t < ‖g x‖ₑ}`;
  `HasWeakTypeOn T D a A μ ν`: `ν {‖T f‖ > t} ≤ (A ‖f‖_{L^a} / t)^a` for `f ∈ D`, `t > 0`;
  `HasStrongTypeOn T D a A μ ν`: `‖T f‖_{L^a} ≤ A ‖f‖_{L^a}` for `f ∈ D`;
  `HasLinftyBoundOn T D B ν`: `‖f‖ ≤ s` everywhere implies `‖T f‖ ≤ B s` `ν`-a.e.
  Constants `A B : ℝ≥0`, exponents are real and enter `eLpNorm` via `ENNReal.ofReal`.
* Measurability of the particular output `T f` is an explicit hypothesis of the main theorems
  (`eLpNorm` of a non-a.e.-strongly-measurable function is `∞`).

## Main results

* `eLpNorm_rpow_eq_lintegral_distributionFunction`: layer-cake formula
  `‖g‖_p^p = p ∫_0^∞ t^(p-1) ν{‖g‖ > t} dt`.
* `HasStrongTypeOn.hasWeakTypeOn`: Chebyshev, strong `(a,a)` implies weak `(a,a)`, same constant.
* `lintegral_rpow_le_of_hasWeakTypeOn`, `eLpNorm_le_of_hasWeakTypeOn_of_pos`: for weak types
  `(a,a)`, `(b,b)` with constants `A`, `B`, `0 < a < p < b < ∞`, and **every** truncation
  parameter `c > 0`,
  `‖T f‖_p^p ≤ p (2^a A^a c^(a-p)/(p-a) + 2^b B^b c^(b-p)/(b-p)) ‖f‖_p^p`
  (`marcinkiewiczBound`).
* `eLpNorm_le_of_hasWeakTypeOn`: the Marcinkiewicz interpolation theorem
  `‖T f‖_p ≤ C(a,b,p) A^(1-θ) B^θ ‖f‖_p`, `1/p = (1-θ)/a + θ/b`, with the explicit finite constant
  `C(a,b,p) = marcinkiewiczConst a b p = (p (2^a/(p-a) + 2^b/(b-p)))^(1/p)`
  (the case `A = 0` or `B = 0` is included).
* `lintegral_rpow_le_of_hasWeakTypeOn_of_linfty`, `eLpNorm_le_of_hasWeakTypeOn_of_linfty_of_pos`,
  `eLpNorm_le_of_hasWeakTypeOn_of_linfty`: the endpoint `b = ∞`,
  `‖T f‖_p ≤ C(a,p) A^(a/p) B^(1-a/p) ‖f‖_p` for `0 < a < p < ∞`, with
  `C(a,p) = marcinkiewiczConstTop a p = 2 (p/(p-a))^(1/p)`.

## Proof

Split `f = f 𝟙_{‖f‖ > c t} + f 𝟙_{‖f‖ ≤ c t}`, use subadditivity and the two weak-type bounds at
height `t/2`, insert into the layer-cake formula and exchange the integrals (Tonelli); the inner
integrals are `∫_0^{‖f‖/c} t^(p-a-1) dt` and `∫_{‖f‖/c}^∞ t^(p-b-1) dt`. Finally optimize `c`.

## References

* J. Marcinkiewicz, *Sur l'interpolation d'opérations*, C. R. Acad. Sci. Paris **208** (1939),
  1272–1273.
* L. Grafakos, *Classical Fourier Analysis*, 3rd ed., Graduate Texts in Mathematics 249,
  Springer, 2014, Theorem 1.3.2.
* E. M. Stein and G. Weiss, *Introduction to Fourier Analysis on Euclidean Spaces*, Chapter V,
  §2.
-/

